# ARK Part Line Metadata

Part classification lives on **part estimate lines** (`repair_order_lines`), not on recommendation status.

## Authority chain

```
Recommendation status (scope)     → customer action / urgency posture
Scope billing posture (scope)     → fees, matrix, labor defaults
Part line metadata (part line)    → source, type, warranty impact on this part
Parts matrix (part line)          → pricing authority
```

## Fields

| Column | Values | Purpose |
|--------|--------|---------|
| `part_source` | `shop_supplied`, `customer_supplied` | Who supplied the part |
| `part_classification` | `oem`, `aftermarket_replacement`, `performance_custom` | What kind of part (nullable until set) |
| `part_warranty_impact` | `none`, `customer_supplied`, `aftermarket_related`, `excluded` | Line-level warranty note |

Defaults: shop supplied, classification unset, warranty impact none.

## UI

Part line entry and inline part edit — **Sourcing** section, below vendor/part number.

Only shown for `type = part`. Not on labor, fee, or note lines.

## Snapshots

Estimate snapshots freeze part metadata labels with the line for document truth.

## Do not

- Move part metadata to recommendation status
- Replace scope billing posture with part warranty impact
- Infer part classification from recommendation status in reports

## Future

Shop-custom classification values (fleet issue, repeat failure) belong in settings authority — not new recommendation statuses.
